                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "32622876",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198160660673",
                            "num_reviews": 237,
                            "playtime_forever": 164,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 162,
                            "last_played": 1605146180
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "TL:DR; Decent game that's hurt by some questionable balancing decisions.\n\n[b]Pros:[/b]\n[list]\n[*] A clean, classic art style\n\n[*] Great boss design\n\n[*] Turn-based combat that feels fun to play\n\n[*] Cool monster-catching mechanic\n\n[*] Costs $4\n\n[/list]\n\n[b]Neutral:[/b]\n[list]\n[*] Simple story\n\n[*] It would be nice if your companion monsters actually leveled up with you\n\n[*] Can build your character the way you want\n\n[*] 2 Hours long\n[/list]\n\n[b]Cons:[/b]\n[list]\n\n[*] Very high encounter rate - This is a huge issue because the game doesn't have healing items/spells and instead intends for you to use the \"rest\" feature. The problem with resting is that it has such a low chance of working and heals for so little that it's basically useless. Increasing defense and power is supposed to mitigate this but rest hardly ever worked at 50 Defense for me. The encounter rate basically forces you to over level in order to survive the huge number of enemies you need to get through just to reach the boss. \n\n[*] Extreme difficulty spike in the last section of the game - Enemy damage gets insanely high before the final boss and it seems like if you're not pumping tons of points into defense then there's no chance of surviving (which basically eliminates replay ability because only a max def. build is viable).\n \n[/list]",
